\ S6d probe J — the ROOTED join asymmetry must stay refused (desk-check A.ii).
\ A Step? dispatch whose Done arm rebuilds the state deriv-free (the nullary
\ helper's push carries no deriv) and whose More arm repacks the remainder
\ (the rooted deriv — the view of the local `a` — rides REQ-4d site 1's
\ construction push). The eliminator's arm merge refuses the asymmetry today;
\ the proposed rootless-only union must NOT admit this shape — the union is
\ conditioned on `owned_root: None`, and this deriv's root is the frame local
\ `a`. The word is declared inline with a Step output so its arms' bare ctors
\ ground via the tail channel, and it is deliberately never called, so the
\ whole pin is the declaration-time check. Clean tree: no impl, no fence —
\ the merge fires as-is, the pin.
import: intrinsics * ;
import: core::prelude * ;
import: hosted::show | . | ;

type: Step['T 'Rest]
| Done
| More 'T 'Rest
;

\ The deriv-free state: a nullary Done whose instantiation the tail channel
\ grounds from the ENCLOSING word's declared output at the splice site (a
\ caller with no declared Step output refuses this word — measured, which is
\ why the asymmetry word below is never called).
: done-empty inline ( -- Step[i64 Slice[i64]] ) Done ;

: rooted-asym inline ( -- Step[i64 Slice[i64]] )
  3 1 fill |a|
  &a slice |va|
  va 7 swap More
  ~[ ( Done ) drop done-empty ]
  ~[ ( More ) More> More ]
  Step? ;
